menu "Gateway: commissioning access point"

    config GW_SOFTAP
        bool "Wi-Fi access point for commissioning (NET-5)"
        depends on GW_WIFI
        default y
        help
            Starts an access point "GW-Setup-XXXXXX" (last bytes of the MAC) when there is no
            valid configuration (rejected, after a factory reset, safe mode, PSRAM fault) and on
            a 2-10 s press of BOOT. WPA2 with the web password (issue #187: the gateway keeps
            only its PMK), or with the device's commissioning password while no web password
            is set; open (no key) only during a claim window (issue #120). The web UI is then
            at the address of the access point (192.168.4.1, the ESP-IDF default): https with
            the default web.https (plain HTTP only redirects), http with web.https false. The
            log line gives the address in use.
            Needs the Wi-Fi driver (CONFIG_GW_WIFI): QEMU has no radio (the emulator build
            runs a simulated access point instead).

    config GW_SOFTAP_TIMEOUT_MIN
        int "Longest time of the access point after a BOOT press in normal mode (min)"
        depends on GW_SOFTAP || GW_IO_SIMULATED
        range 1 1440
        default 30
        help
            With a valid configuration, the access point stops at the end of this time, also
            with a client. In the modes without a valid configuration there is no longest time:
            only GW_SOFTAP_IDLE_MIN stops it.

    config GW_SOFTAP_IDLE_MIN
        int "Minutes without a client that stop the access point (issue #187)"
        depends on GW_SOFTAP || GW_IO_SIMULATED
        range 1 60
        default 5
        help
            The access point stops after this time without a client, in every mode (normal,
            recovery, commissioning, safe mode, PSRAM fault). The time counts from the start
            and from the moment the last client leaves. A new BOOT press of 2-10 s starts the
            access point again.

endmenu
